From 78e35b123bea9110b52b66c154d59ee8219cbb1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viktor Semenov <suit.uanic@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 23:47:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/45] Let a Specula player command an unassigned slot of a
 hosted game

-autostart-specula-play (autostart_specula_play.js, chosen in
entrypoint.js) hosts a game as an observer and launches it once its own
assignment exists, with -autostart-players slots and the web player's
left unassigned. The feed socket now also reads an uplink from the
encoder: kind 1 records are simulation commands for a player, which
CNetClientTurnManager posts after each turn's feed, and kind 2 records
are the placement queries (SetBuildingPlacementPreview,
GetFoundationSnapData, SetWallPlacementPreview), answered between turns
in feed record 23. Template data names the VisualActor a preview draws,
and kind 21 adds the ceasefire end.

NetServer lets the controller command a player that no enabled
assignment holds, as 54619460d4 does, for unassigned slots only. A
nonvisual host now runs its turns in real time and sleeps 1 ms a frame,
where it ran as fast as it could. The feed stays v14.
